  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sea kelp and peppermint soap is a clean-scented cold-process bar with a subtle marine mineral quality from finely powdered kelp and a brisk, cooling edge from peppermint essential oil. The coconut, olive, and shea base gives a firm, long-lasting bar with a generous, conditioning lather. The kelp distributes as tiny dark flecks through the finished bar. Seven bars; ready after 4-6 weeks."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ingredients"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 1,
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "coconut-oil",
              "amount": 315,
              "unit": "g",
              "isOptional": false,
              "prepNote": "45% of oil weight; lather and hardness"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "olive-oil",
              "amount": 245,
              "unit": "g",
              "isOptional": false,
              "prepNote": "pure (not extra virgin); 35% of oil weight; conditioning base"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "shea-butter",
              "amount": 140,
              "unit": "g",
              "isOptional": false,
              "prepNote": "20% of oil weight; skin conditioning and creaminess"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "sodium-hydroxide",
              "amount": 103,
              "unit": "g",
              "isOptional": false,
              "prepNote": "NaOH at 99% purity; calculated for 5% superfat"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "distilled-water",
              "amount": 224,
              "unit": "g",
              "isOptional": false,
              "prepNote": "32% of oil weight; the lye solution liquid"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "essential-oil-peppermint",
              "amount": 21,
              "unit": "g",
              "isOptional": false,
              "prepNote": "3% of oil weight; added at trace; bright and cooling"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "kelp-powder",
              "amount": 3.5,
              "unit": "g",
              "isOptional": false,
              "prepNote": "cosmetic-grade sea kelp powder; 0.5% of oil weight; added at trace for mineral content and natural green tint"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make the lye solution"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Put on protective gloves and goggles. Work in a ventilated space. Add the sodium hydroxide slowly to the distilled water in the HDPE pitcher, stirring until dissolved. Cool to 38-42°C."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Prepare the oils"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Melt the coconut oil and shea butter together, then add the olive oil. Bring to 38-42°C."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Blend to trace and add botanicals"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pour the lye solution into the oils. Stick-blend in short bursts until the batter reaches light ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "trace",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                        "attrs": {
                          "termSlug": "trace"
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Stir in the peppermint essential oil and the kelp powder by hand. Mix until evenly distributed."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pour into the mould. Insulate and leave 24-48 hours. Unmould, cut into 7 bars wearing gloves, and cure on a rack for 4-6 weeks."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "saponification",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                        "attrs": {
                          "termSlug": "saponification"
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " is complete when a corner touched to the tongue gives no 'zap' sensation. The bars turn from dark green-flecked to lighter as they cure."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Storage and shelf life"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Store cured bars on a ventilated rack in a cool, dry place. The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "superfat",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "superfat"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " from the shea butter keeps the bar conditioning for the full 2-year shelf life. Discard if orange spots appear (DOS) or the bar smells rancid."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
